* mje15033.lib - onsemi MJE15033, PNP complementary silicon power
* transistor, TO-220, 250 V / 8.0 A / 50 W.
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_pnp/mje15033.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter Qmje15033
*
* NOTE THE MODEL NAME: Qmje15033, not MJE15033, exactly as the vendor
* wrote it.
*
* Role in this project: the PNP half of the complementary Class A emitter
* follower that forms the output stage of the gain block
* (circuits/preamp/gain_block.py:368). One instance per block, the
* complement of models/bjt_npn/mje15032.lib.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_pnp/mje15033.provenance.json, the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_pnp/onsemi/MJE15033/PROVENANCE.json, and the reasoning in
* docs/preamp/reports/2026-09-10-L24-t7-dispositivi-attivi.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Frozen byte-for-byte from onsemi's own /download/models/lib/mje15033.lib
* and copied here unchanged: nothing removed, no value rounded, reordered
* or "corrected", model name left as served.
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_pnp/onsemi/MJE15033/mje15033.lib) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_pnp/mje15033.lib)      # empty
*
* Same contractor authorship as its NPN complement - "Model Generated by
* MODPEX / Copyright(c) Symmetry Design Systems", 1 February 2004,
* PSpice format - recorded rather than hidden, for the reason given in
* the MJE15032 header.
*
* ONE GAP IS DECLARED AND NOT FILLED, and it belongs to the part rather
* than to the model: onsemi has NO PRODUCT PAGE for MJE15033G, so its
* lifecycle status under T8 rests on the ordering table of a December
* 2024 datasheet ("orderable"), not on an explicit Active string. Its NPN
* complement is Active on a real product page. ADR-017 lists this among
* the conditions that reopen the decision.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET - hFE CLEAN, fT IS NOT
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Datasheet MJE15032/D, December 2024 Rev. 7, frozen at
* vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE15032/mje15032-d.pdf (the two devices share
* one document, which is why the PNP's directory holds no PDF of its
* own). ngspice 47, set temp = 25 (the datasheet is @ 25 C, ngspice
* defaults to 27):
*
*   hFE @ IC = 0.5 A, VCE = -5 V      88.218       70 MIN.     inside
*   hFE @ IC = 1.0 A, VCE = -5 V      66.917       50 MIN.     inside
*   hFE @ IC = 2.0 A, VCE = -5 V      42.766       10 MIN.     inside
*   fT  @ IC = 500 mA, VCE = -10 V,
*       ftest = 1.0 MHz               29.286 MHz   30 MHz MIN. ***OUTSIDE***
*
* On hFE this is the clean half of the output stage: the NPN MJE15032
* misses its own 70 minimum at 0.5 A by 5.1% (NC-024), this one clears
* it by 26%.
*
* ON fT IT IS NOT CLEAN, and this is new in L25 - it is NC-025, shared
* with the NPN. Note 2 of the datasheet defines fT as "hfe ftest" and
* the test row gives ftest = 1.0 MHz, so fT is the gain-bandwidth
* product measured AT 1 MHz. Measured that way, with IC verified to
* 500.000 mA, this model gives 29.286 MHz against a 30 MHz minimum -
* 2.4% short. (The |hfe| = 1 crossing gives 30.719 MHz and would clear
* it; that is the wrong comparison, because the minimum is written
* against the 1 MHz test.) L24 recorded 31.38 MHz and read it as inside.
*
* Direction: the model is SLOWER than the guaranteed part, so figures
* computed with it are pessimistic - the safe direction, and the same
* shape as NC-020 on the LS352. The NPN misses by 7.8%, this one by
* 2.4%.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE NUMBERS THE DATASHEET DOES NOT GIVE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* The project runs this device at 14.71 mA (gain_block.py:434), 34 times
* below the lowest specified point. There the model says:
*
*   hFE @ 15 mA      129.38       (re-measured in L25)
*   fT  @ 15 mA      12.58 MHz    (L24's figure, NOT re-measured here)
*
* hFE 129.4 here against 75.7 on the NPN is a 1.7x IMBALANCE inside a
* complementary follower. The hand-written placeholders could not show it
* - they were symmetric by construction - and it is Fase 4 material.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT THIS MODEL DOES NOT HAVE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* NO FLICKER NOISE FROM THE MANUFACTURER: KF=0, AF=1 in the vendor line,
* which is the same thing as having none. Since L44 (ADR-057) a declared
* upper bound, KF = 1e-13 AF = 1.4, is appended at the END of this file,
* outside the vendor block, and overrides it.
*
* No SPICE magnitude suffix appears in the model line, so
* docs/limitations.md #13 has nothing to bite on here.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* BELOW THIS LINE: THE VENDOR FILE, BYTE FOR BYTE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
**************************************
*      Model Generated by MODPEX     *
*Copyright(c) Symmetry Design Systems*
*         All Rights Reserved        *
*    UNPUBLISHED LICENSED SOFTWARE   *
*   Contains Proprietary Information *
*      Which is The Property of      *
*     SYMMETRY OR ITS LICENSORS      *
*    Modeling services provided by   *
* Interface Technologies www.i-t.com *
**************************************
.MODEL Qmje15033 pnp
+IS=7.51228e-10 BF=134.35 NF=1.25737 VAF=12.5778
+IKF=1.88497 ISE=7.74267e-12 NE=3.34528 BR=5.14173
+NR=1.47488 VAR=1.4505 IKR=7.47186 ISC=3.25e-13
+NC=4 RB=4.37743 IRB=0.1 RBM=0.1
+RE=0.000332989 RC=0.381218 XTB=0.223027 XTI=1
+EG=1.05 CJE=3.06005e-09 VJE=0.64838 MJE=0.352991
+TF=4.78203e-09 XTF=1.50001 VTF=1.00006 ITF=0.999988
+CJC=3.00101e-10 VJC=0.600019 MJC=0.409916 XCJC=0.8
+FC=0.534975 CJS=0 VJS=0.75 MJS=0.5
+TR=1e-07 PTF=0 KF=0 AF=1
* Model generated on Feb  1, 2004
* Model format: PSpice
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* L44 (ADR-057): FLICKER NOISE ADDED - NOT FROM THE MANUFACTURER
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* The '+' line at the very end CONTINUES the .MODEL card above: ngspice
* joins it to the last card and skips the comment lines in between, and
* when a parameter repeats the LAST value wins. Measured in L44, not
* assumed, and re-measured on every run by the [flicker] check in
* scripts/validate_models.py (base-current noise, KF read back from
* S(10 Hz) - S(10 kHz)). It sits OUTSIDE the vendor block so that the
* vendor bytes stay exactly as served: the non-comment diff against the
* file under vendor/ is this one line and nothing else.
*
* WHAT THE NUMBERS ARE. ngspice: i_n^2 = 2 q Ib + KF Ib^AF / f. KF = 1e-13
* with AF = 1.4 is a DECLARED UPPER BOUND for the small-signal bipolar
* class, not a fit to this part. Sources (PDFs and readings under vendor/,
* PROVENANCE files next to them):
*   - 2N5087, Motorola, Fig. 2 p. 3 (vendor/bjt_pnp/motorola/2N5087/):
*     AF = 1.35 consistent over 10 uA..1 mA, KF ~2e-14 at 10 Hz, ~5e-14
*     at 300 Hz;
*   - Linear Systems databook, "Solving the Noise Puzzle", Fig. 3 p. 329
*     (LS310/LS350 family): AF ~1.46, KF ~6e-14; worst case ~2x typical.
*   Typical class value 5e-14; the bound is 2x that.
*
* FOR THIS PART THERE IS NO CURVE, and none was found for any power
* bipolar: the bound is applied by DECLARED CHOICE. The L44 scan shows it
* does not matter here - the output stage moves E5 by < 0.001 uV even
* with a 100 kHz 1/f corner. The vendor card's own KF=0 AF=1 is
* overridden by the line below.
* What it buys: E5 with this bound on every bipolar device is 5.53 uV
* worst case against 9.95 (5.1 dB margin); a bound 10x higher still gives
* 8.57 uV. data/2026-10-01/L44/, report 2026-10-01-L44-rumore-1f.md.
+ KF=1e-13 AF=1.4
